bc19fb34fa25ad03e8ee9abfbbb9da71eb4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/media-specs.md","size":4367,"sha256":"767ec3358df14fe7856fc73483579a698035b1ab4c81d5229187e69add784f58","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/platform-controls.md","size":15761,"sha256":"27447e46333349ffa4a14b9e11d1103a45ebbc85d6586340e14a666b5ac707f8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/upload-flow.md","size":6023,"sha256":"407092d9a9dfbd9b961142e2eddf1859963f0c547e38594060540f2c2d41245c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2080,"sha256":"e2c98bb5c84c13b241cbff1aca0ebb56e2f1a63ccc3a72512892781546470550","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1791462949112,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c068100c6cf125760b4ecd7b9383ff8622ed92b3c8e58b0fc6bb76e42b796645","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c068100c6cf125760b4ecd7b9383ff8622ed92b3c8e58b0fc6bb76e42b796645","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1791462742199},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":87,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":45,"checkedAt":1791462949112},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed PostFast API guide for managing social media posts, with high-impact actions like posting, deleting, and comment moderation that users should confirm carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of POSTFAST_API_KEY, PostFast API calls, and signed S3 uploads is proportionate to a SaaS social-media management skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The package appears to be markdown and JSON documentation/examples only; no executable installer, dependency setup, or local hooks were found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill explicitly warns to confirm destructive or public-facing actions and to preview delete targets, though its filter-driven bulk-delete workflow remains high impact if used carelessly.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No local persistence or privilege escalation was found; persistent effects are remote business actions such as scheduled posts, deleted PostFast records, replies, moderation state, and generated connect links.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The capabilities match the stated purpose: scheduling, uploading media, analytics, account connection links, deleting posts, and social inbox moderation through PostFast.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust PostFast with the connected social accounts and API key. Confirm any action that publishes, replies, hides, deletes, bulk-deletes, or sends a connect link, and review exact targets and filters before approving destructive operations.","findings":"[TM1] expected: Delete and bulk-delete endpoints are explicit content-management features. The main skill states deletion is immediate, requires listing candidates and waiting for a yes unless exact IDs were provided, and the delete-all loop is tied to prior user confirmation.\n[E1] expected: External transmission to api.postfa.st and signed upload URLs is the core integration behavior, not hidden exfiltration; the skill declares POSTFAST_API_KEY and warns that connect links should be treated like credentials.\n[SQP-1] expected: The bulk-delete example documents a repeat-until-empty workflow, but also says to confirm with the user before sending; users should still review filter scope before any repeated deletion.\n[SQP-2] expected: The reference and example docs describe destructive deletion, while the main skill provides clearer irreversibility and confirmation guidance; this is a guidance gap, not evidence of hidden behavior.\n[SQP-3] expected: The YouTube captions example hard-codes English sample content and youtubeLanguage 'en'; this is a sample localization limitation rather than a security issue.\n[aig-skill-scan] expected: The supplied A.I.G. SARIF contained no findings.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791462949112}}}}}